0..73 Comment "//! A frame-region buffer orphaned: abandoning a task whose stack holds a"
74..154 Comment "//! pending completion may hand the completion, buffer inside, to a reactor that"
155..230 Comment "//! reaps it later [boats-2020-notes_on_io_uring]. That is sound only for a"
231..306 Comment "//! buffer the reactor\'s region outlives, never one living in the abandoned"
307..317 Comment "//! frame."
318..321 Comment "//!"
322..359 Comment "//! - see: #1183 — `bufferOrphaned`"
360..403 Comment "//! - cites: [boats-2020-notes_on_io_uring]"
404..407 Comment "//!"
408..507 Comment "//! [boats-2020-notes_on_io_uring]: https://without.boats/blog/io-uring/ \"boats, Notes on io-uring\""
509..548 Comment "// The ring\'s protocol and its entries."
549..555 Keyword "import"
556..557 StringLit "\""
557..595 StringLit "../../model/completion/ring-base.gandr"
595..596 StringLit "\""
596..597 Other ";"
599..670 Comment "/// A pending completion handed to a reaping peer while its frame ends."
671..749 Comment "/// Delegation admits the handover, and nothing ties the buffer to a region. A"
750..823 Comment "/// kernel handed a buffer kept in a hold\'s region is refused where it is"
824..899 Comment "/// forked, since no region bounds a forked peer (`region-ended.gandr`), so"
900..967 Comment "/// this checks until a kernel can be bounded by the buffer\'s hold,"
968..1029 Comment "/// when a reaper that outlives the hold becomes the refusal."
